{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZb7wpATG2fSe9HcDAB1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9`\n- ShipmentController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:20`\n- ShipmentRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:11`\n- Error exceptions: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:11`\n- Error codes: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31`\n- Global exception handler: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13`\n- Tests: `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt:23`\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Controllers throw `ConflictException` and `ResourceNotFoundException` subclasses instead of returning error ResponseEntity\n2. Exceptions carry an `ErrorCode` enum value\n3. Central `GlobalExceptionHandler` handles all `ApiException` subclasses and formats them consistently\n4. Tests use MockMvc with status matchers and jsonPath assertions\n5. In-memory repository using ConcurrentHashMap for quick startup\n6. POST endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(resource)`\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` - Add new `ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` for confirming cancelled shipments\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add POST endpoint for confirm operation\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add tests for confirm operation (4 test cases)\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Not implementing idempotency correctly (second confirm of CONFIRMED shipment must not fail)\n2. Wrong HTTP status code for cancelled/invalid transitions\n3. Failing to persist the state change in repository\n4. Breaking existing tests by changing controller structure\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone. The requirement is clear on all error cases and expected behavior.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`** - Add new error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to the `ErrorCode` enum to represent when a shipment cannot be transitioned to a new state (e.g., confirming a CANCELLED shipment).\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`** - Add a new method `confirm()` that:\n   - Maps to `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`\n   - Takes `shipmentId` as path parameter\n   - Retrieves the shipment or throws `ResourceNotFoundException` with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`\n   - If status is CREATED: updates status to CONFIRMED, saves, returns 200 with the shipment\n   - If status is CONFIRMED: returns 200 with the shipment unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED: throws `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` (409)\n   - Returns `ResponseEntity.ok(updatedShipment)`\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** - Add four new test methods:\n   - Test 1: Confirm a CREATED shipment → 200, status becomes CONFIRMED\n   - Test 2: Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment → 200, status stays CONFIRMED (idempotency)\n   - Test 3: Confirm a CANCELLED shipment → 409 with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` error code\n   - Test 4: Confirm a non-existent shipment → 404 with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` error code\n\n**Alternative rejected and why:**\n\nI considered not adding a new error code and reusing `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` with a different message, but that violates the convention that error codes describe *what happened* not the message prose. The error code should be stable for machine-readable switching. Adding `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` is more general and future-proof if other invalid state transitions are added.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED):** \n  - Read: Shipment from repository\n  - Write: Updated shipment with CONFIRMED status\n  - Return: 200 OK with shipment\n  \n- **Idempotent path (already CONFIRMED):** \n  - Read: Shipment from repository (already CONFIRMED)\n  - Write: No change (status already CONFIRMED)\n  - Return: 200 OK with unchanged shipment\n  \n- **Cancelled rejection:** \n  - Read: Shipment from repository (status is CANCELLED)\n  - Write: None\n  - Return: 409 Conflict with error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS`\n  - Exception: `ConflictException`\n  \n- **Not found:** \n  - Read: Repository returns null\n  - Write: None\n  - Return: 404 Not Found with error code `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`\n  - Exception: `ResourceNotFoundException`\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: Confirm CREATED shipment** - Create S-1 (auto CREATED), POST confirm, verify status 200 and shipment has CONFIRMED status\n2. **Test: Idempotent confirm** - Create S-2 (auto CREATED), confirm twice, both should succeed with 200 and CONFIRMED status\n3. **Test: Confirm CANCELLED shipment** - Manually set shipment to CANCELLED in repository, POST confirm, verify 409 and error code\n4. **Test: Confirm missing shipment** - POST confirm to non-existent S-missing, verify 404 and error code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes according to the design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1284,"cache_read_input_tokens":17441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1284},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"85e217db-d451-4839-9afb-dd025682a38d","uuid":"d7b485da-4f41-4082-bbaa-57c4e69efbe6","timestamp":"2026-09-30T12:02:05.954Z","request_id":"req_011CfZb7wRb7QjAKDcbVtWdm"}
